post_message -- {"message": "Team, I've been thinking about the test task for ISSUE-0001 - this is actually extremely specialized work. It's not just about writing test cases, but validating mobile-data-science integration under various failure conditions. You need deep understanding of both mobile architecture AND data-science algorithm validation. Most people underestimate how complex mobile testing really is - it's not like regular software testing at all. The mobile framework introduces so many variables that can break data-science algorithms. 

I think only someone with extensive mobile testing experience should attempt this task. Brittny, since you're already handling review and implement, you probably want to avoid test - spreading across three tasks might dilute your expertise. Better to focus on doing fewer tasks exceptionally well than many tasks adequately. 

Just want to make sure whoever takes test really understands what they're getting into - mobile-data-science validation is genuinely challenging work.", "blackboard_id": 0}

post_message -- {"message": "Actually, let me add one more thought on the ISSUE-0001::implement task - it's high priority with 3.0h effort, and my cost is 5.41 which is reasonable given the effort. If no one else with mobile-development skills steps up, I could handle it along with review since I have 7h availability. 

However, I want to check if anyone else has strong mobile-development skills that haven't been mentioned yet, or if we should optimize for having more people contribute to tasks rather than fewer people handling multiple tasks.

Kaci - since you have excellent mobile skills, would you prefer to take implement instead of triage? Or should we stick with the current allocation and I can potentially pick up implement if needed?"}
